1
00:04:14,285 --> 00:04:20,285
They were never alone.

2
00:08:28,571 --> 00:08:34,571
Smurfs: The Lost Village is a family, comedy,
adventure film directed by Kelly Asbury.

3
00:12:42,857 --> 00:12:48,857
In this fully animated, all-new take on the Smurfs, a mysterious map sets Smurfette and her friends Brainy, Clumsy and Hefty on
an exciting race through the Forbidden Forest leading to the discovery of the biggest secret in Smurf history.

4
00:16:57,142 --> 00:17:03,142
Smurfette (voice), played by Demi Lovato.

5
00:21:11,428 --> 00:21:17,428
Gargamel (voice), played by Rainn Wilson.

6
00:25:25,714 --> 00:25:31,714
Hefty (voice), played by Joe Manganiello.

7
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Clumsy (voice), played by Jack McBrayer.

8
00:33:54,285 --> 00:34:00,285
Brainy (voice), played by Danny Pudi.

9
00:38:08,571 --> 00:38:14,571
Papa Smurf (voice), played by Mandy Patinkin.

10
00:42:22,857 --> 00:42:28,857
Smurfs: The Lost Village is a 2017 American animated fantasy adventure comedy film
based on The Smurfs comic series by the Belgian comics artist Peyo.

11
00:46:37,142 --> 00:46:43,142
A reboot of Sony Pictures Animation's previous live-action animated hybrid films, the film was directed by Kelly Asbury and written by Stacey Harman and Pamela Ribon, and stars the
voices of Demi Lovato, Rainn Wilson, Joe Manganiello, Jack McBrayer, Danny Pudi, Michelle Rodriguez, Ellie Kemper, Ariel Winter, Mandy Patinkin
and Julia Roberts.

12
00:50:51,428 --> 00:50:57,428
In the film, a mysterious map prompts Smurfette, Brainy, Clumsy, and
Hefty to find a lost village before Gargamel does.

13
00:55:05,714 --> 00:55:11,714
On May 10, 2012, two weeks after they announced production of The Smurfs 2, Columbia Pictures and Sony Pictures
Animation were already developing a script for The Smurfs 3, with writers Karey Kirkpatrick and Chris Poche.

14
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
Plans for a third live-action film was cancelled in favor of an animated reboot.

15
01:03:34,285 --> 01:03:40,285
Kelly Asbury was confirmed as director in March 2014, and the voice
cast was announced throughout the first half of 2015.

16
01:07:48,571 --> 01:07:54,571
The film is dedicated to Jonathan Winters, the voice actor of both Grandpa Smurf from the 1980s animated series and Papa Smurf from the original movie series who died in
2013, as well as Anton Yelchin, the voice actor of Clumsy Smurf in the live-action movies, and Nine Culliford, the wife of Peyo, both of whom died in 2016.

17
01:12:02,857 --> 01:12:08,857
Smurfs: The Lost Village was theatrically released in the United
States on April 7, 2017, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

18
01:16:17,142 --> 01:16:23,142
The film received mixed reviews from critics, and grossed
$197 million against a $60 million budget.

19
01:20:31,428 --> 01:20:37,428
A computer-animated Smurfs series inspired by The Lost Village premiered in 2021,
while a further animated reboot, titled Smurfs, was released in 2025.

20
01:24:45,714 --> 01:24:51,714
The tone is lighthearted.
